# Keep the build context small and free of anything private.
#
# Unfiltered this repo is ~13 GB, almost all of it overlay/src-tauri/target, and docker uploads the
# whole context to the daemon before the first instruction runs. It also picks up .env, which on a
# developer machine holds real API keys and must never be baked into an image.

# Secrets and local config.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build output and caches, all regenerated inside the container.
**/target/
**/node_modules/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
dist/
overlay/dist/
.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/

# Local state: databases and anything the app wrote while running.
backend/data/
**/*.sqlite3

# Not needed to build, and a stale .git is a large upload for nothing.
.git/
.git.broken-*/
.github/
.claude/

# Tests and eval harness; the package ships neither.
backend/tests/
backend/eval/

# Notes and docs.
docs/
*.md
!LICENSE
ideas.txt
TODO.md
